---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/07-12/',dims='https://www.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/manuals/MAN0010405_QuantStudio_3_5_Sys_SPG.pdf#page=6',photo='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/manuals/MAN0010407_QuantStudio_3_5_InstallUseMaint_UG.pdf#page=1';
---
<Layout pageTitle="QuantStudio 3 sealed cabinet and detached geometry cards" description="Orbit the inert QuantStudio 3 exterior and compare triangle annotations on unrelated, preauthored geometry cards." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="qs3"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/07-12/">← Equipment 07-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#qs-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">07-12 / SEALED DOCUMENTARY EXTERIOR · DETACHED LINE DRAWINGS</p><h2>Three points don’t always enclose an area</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect the closed QuantStudio 3 cabinet, then use an unrelated classroom card to compare a triangle with three points on a line.</p></header>
<div class="qs-cols"><section><h3>Unpowered cabinet</h3><canvas id="qs-model" aria-label="Orbitable sealed QuantStudio 3 and physically separate educational stand"></canvas><p id="qs-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="qs-front">Reset overview</button><button id="qs-rear">Rear exterior</button><button id="qs-board">Detached card</button></section>
<section><h3>Independent annotation cards</h3><label>Fixed drawing<select id="qs-card"><option value="triangle">A · right triangle</option><option value="flat">B · three points in a line</option></select></label><button id="qs-next">Switch card</button>
<svg id="qs-diagram" viewBox="0 0 150 116" role="img" aria-label="A preauthored triangle or line annotated with points A, B and C"><rect width="150" height="116" fill="#20343a"/><polygon id="qs-annotation" stroke="#ffc571" stroke-width="1.2"/><g fill="#e0f4ea" stroke="#20343a" stroke-width=".7"><circle id="qs-p0" r="3"/><circle id="qs-p1" r="3"/><circle id="qs-p2" r="3"/></g><g fill="#e8e9dc" font-size="11" font-family="system-ui"><text id="qs-l0">A</text><text id="qs-l1">B</text><text id="qs-l2">C</text></g></svg>
<p id="qs-readout" role="status"></p><p>AB / BC / CA: <strong id="qs-sides"></strong>. Both cards have three marked points. Only card A bounds a region.</p><button id="qs-export">Download annotation summary</button><p><a href={d+'example-geometry.json'}>Example for card A</a>. No device, specimen or measurement interface is involved.</p></section></div>
<section id="qs-evidence"><h3>Selected housing and checks</h3><div class="qs-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original closed QuantStudio 3 model, blank screen and detached geometry card"/><figcaption>Original three-quarter view. The <a href={photo}>Applied Biosystems MAN0010407 D.0 cover image, left unit</a> establishes the QuantStudio 3's tall, curved white body, indigo trim, fixed sloped screen and flush lower front.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={d+'rear.webp'} alt="Original inferred rear panel and continuous white QuantStudio 3 housing"/><figcaption>Original rear, simplified and sealed. The <a href={dims}>MAN0010405 E physical-envelope table</a> gives 270 × 400 × 500 mm (W × H × D). Face details, seams, feet and rear panel are inferred; no working internals or connectivity.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual / tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exterior envelope</td><td>270 × 400 × 500 mm</td><td>Modeled within 1.5 mm; no installation survey</td></tr><tr><td>A: perpendicular legs 8 and 6</td><td>Hypotenuse 10; 24 square units</td><td>Exact</td></tr><tr><td>B: aligned points at 0, 5 and 8</td><td>Edge lengths 5 / 3 / 8; no enclosed region</td><td>Exact</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The independent drawing computes edge distance and half the absolute cross product of two sides. Nothing in this exhibit models acquisitions, assays, sample handling, instrument operation or data analysis. The register’s original acceptance is unsupported.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'quantstudio3.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'geometry-card.mjs'}>Geometry actions and report</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR target bounds</a>. Headset use not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/07-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#qs3 .qs-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#qs3 section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#qs3 :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .25rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#qs3 button{cursor:pointer}#qs3 :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#qs-model{width:100%;height:354px;display:block;touch-action:none}#qs-diagram{width:min(100%,340px);display:block;margin:.45rem auto}#qs3 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#qs3 figure img{width:100%}
#qs3 table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#qs3 td,#qs3 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#qs3 .qs-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#qs-model{height:282px}}
</style>
